<title>Network.fetchFile Action</title>


<subheader>Format</subheader>

<logicsyntax>
s = CS.Network.fetchFile (<arg>url</arg> := ..., <arg>path</arg> := ...
                       『, <arg>method</arg> := ...』
                       『, <arg>headers</arg> := ...』
                       『, <arg>body</arg> := ...』『, <arg>bodyFormat</arg> := ...』
                       『, <arg>detailed</arg> := ...』
                       『, <arg>responseHeadersFormat</arg> := ...』)
</logicsyntax>

<indent><table 3 header nowrap>
    <cell>Argument</cell><cell>Description</cell><cell nowrap>Types / Required</cell>
    <cell><arg>url</arg></cell><cell>The URL to fetch.</cell><cell>string~!~required</cell>
    <cell><arg>path</arg></cell><cell>The path of the file to create from the fetched content.</cell><cell>string~!~required</cell>
    <include fetch_arguments_optional.hgi />
</table></indent>


<subheader>Description</subheader>

The <action>Network.fetchFile</action> <link action_invoker.csdoc>action</link> submits a HTTP request to a server and writes the response to the disk, potentially also returning response details. The file is written to a file specified as <arg>path</arg>. If a file already exists at <arg>path</arg>, it is overwritten with the new contents.

This action is a wrapper around the actions <action>Network.fetch</action> and <action>Network.fetchBody</action>. <include fetch_convenience_methods.hgi />


<include fetch_url.hgi />

<include fetch_method.hgi />

<include fetch_headers.hgi />

<include fetch_body.hgi />

<include fetch_detailed_response.hgi />


<subheader>Return Value</subheader>

By default, the action writes the response to the disk and returns the fully evaluated path of the written file. If <arg>detailed</arg> is <logiccolor>true</logiccolor>, the action returns an object with the response "body" as the file path and details about the response as described above.


<subheader>Exceptions</subheader>

The action throws an exception if any of its arguments are not specified in a valid form, or if:

<list>
    <include fetch_exceptions.hgi />
    <li>The file cannot be created or fully written.</li>
</list>


<subheader>Example (CSPro Logic)</subheader>

<logic>
string imagesBaseUrl = "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/csprousers/cspro/refs/heads/dev/cspro/html/images/";
string imageFilename = "cspro-logo-medium.png";

string downloadedImageFilePath = CS.Network.fetchFile(
    url := imagesBaseUrl + imageFilename,
    path := imageFilename
);

view(downloadedImageFilePath);
</logic>


<seealso CS_Network.csdoc />
